# L set, kernel 27. Parker, Zavalishin and Le Bivic, DAFx-16: triangular (linear) kernel, eq. (14), with the fallbacks
# of eqs. (15)-(16), on the hard clipper eq. (24): F0 from eq. (25), F1 (antiderivative of x f(x)) from eq. (26):
# F1 = x^3/3 for |x| <= 1, (x^2/2 - 1/6) sgn(x) otherwise.
#   y = [xn (F0(xn) - F0(xn-1)) - (F1(xn) - F1(xn-1))] / (xn - xn-1)^2
#     + [xn-2 (F0(xn-2) - F0(xn-1)) - (F1(xn-2) - F1(xn-1))] / (xn-2 - xn-1)^2
# Fallbacks: first term -> f((xn + 2 xn-1)/3)/2, second -> f((xn-2 + 2 xn-1)/3)/2. Threshold 0.01: the 1/(dx)^2 terms lose float32 precision for smaller steps (the paper, sec. 3.1, warns of this ill-conditioning).
# F0 and F1 are computed once per sample and their past values reused through delay(), as the paper suggests (sec. 3).
x0 = in * 6.0
x1 = delay(x0, 1)
x2 = delay(x0, 2)
p0 = if(abs(x0) <= 1.0, 0.5 * x0 * x0, abs(x0) - 0.5)
r0 = if(abs(x0) <= 1.0, x0 * x0 * x0 / 3.0, (0.5 * x0 * x0 - 0.166667) * if(x0 < 0, -1.0, 1.0))
p1 = delay(p0, 1)
p2 = delay(p0, 2)
r1 = delay(r0, 1)
r2 = delay(r0, 2)
da = x0 - x1
db = x2 - x1
sa = if(abs(da) < 0.01, 1.0, da * da)
sb = if(abs(db) < 0.01, 1.0, db * db)
ta = if(abs(da) < 0.01, 0.5 * clamp((x0 + 2.0 * x1) / 3.0, -1.0, 1.0), (x0 * (p0 - p1) - (r0 - r1)) / sa)
tb = if(abs(db) < 0.01, 0.5 * clamp((x2 + 2.0 * x1) / 3.0, -1.0, 1.0), (x2 * (p2 - p1) - (r2 - r1)) / sb)
out = (ta + tb) * 0.5
